text:
anita: quick note from QA: Java sample app shows intermittent hang + 504s when token refresh happens under load on Android 15. Happens with Retrofit/OkHttp default sample.

omar: any chance it's the classic interceptor -> refresh -> same client reentrancy?

anita: yup. sample uses synchronized refresh in Interceptor which calls Retrofit service (same OkHttp client). we see dispatcher queue growth.

peter: can you paste the code snippet?

anita: snippet from sample: 
```java
@Override public Response intercept(Chain chain) throws IOException {
  String t = tokenStore.get();
  if (t == null) {
    synchronized(lock) {
      if (tokenStore.get() == null) tokenStore.set(refreshBlocking());
      t = tokenStore.get();
    }
  }
  Request req = chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer " + t).build();
  Response r = chain.proceed(req);
  if (r.code() == 401) {
    synchronized(lock) { tokenStore.set(refreshBlocking()); }
    return chain.proceed(req.newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer " + tokenStore.get()).build());
  }
  return r;
}
```

omar: that will consume Dispatcher threads while refreshBlocking uses the same client -> thread starvation. on Android 15 HTTP/2 prioritization changes made it surface as 504s rather than just slow responses.

peter: two low-friction fixes: 1) use a dedicated "refreshClient" (no auth interceptors, tiny dispatcher: maxRequests=2, maxRequestsPerHost=1, small connection pool); 2) add an in-flight dedupe (singleflight) so only one refresh runs. For Java we prefer CompletableFuture singleflight.

anita: we also saw token endpoint 429s from the server because multiple threads hit refresh concurrently after network flaps. singleflight + backoff fixed that.

omar: another tip: set retryOnConnectionFailure(false) for long-lived streaming calls in sample, so they don't endlessly retry and hold connections. add readTimeout/callTimeout tuned for mobile.

peter: can someone add a small Java sample for CompletableFuture singleflight into the repo? I can convert to Kotlin Deferred later. gist idea: 
```java
private final AtomicReference<CompletableFuture<Token>> inflight = new AtomicReference<>();
public Token refreshSingleflight() {
  for (;;) {
    CompletableFuture<Token> cur = inflight.get();
    if (cur != null) return cur.join();
    CompletableFuture<Token> f = CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> refreshBlocking());
    if (inflight.compareAndSet(null, f)) {
      try { return f.join(); } finally { inflight.compareAndSet(f, null); }
    }
  }
}
```

anita: implemented that plus refreshClient in sample branch and QA says repro disappeared locally. opening PR.

omar: please add a README note: "Do not call same OkHttp client from inside an interceptor or Authenticator; use a separate client for token endpoint and de-duplicate refreshes." mention Android 15 HTTP/2 behavior as footnote.

peter: also add a small integration test that spawns 20 parallel requests and toggles airplane mode to simulate flakiness. CI should catch regressions.

sdk-ci: CI checklist: include unit + integration, ensure flaky test is annotated and can be skipped on older devices.

